    "narrative": "Our lineup today is anchored by **Lawrence Butler**, whose score of 66.98 makes him our only truly \"Strong\" play. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive 13% boost against a right-handed matchup and a park factor that clearly favors his profile, positioning him as the centerpiece of our production today. While **Cal Raleigh** (58.45), **Masyn Winn** (56.37), and **Luis Arraez** (55.83) fall into the high-end of our \"Marginal\" bucket, they remain viable starts. **Luis Arraez** in particular is buoyed by a 10% boost for hitting at the top of the order, offsetting a slight negative platoon edge against a lefty, while **Masyn Winn** benefits from the highest SP skill advantage in our lineup (+13%), mitigating the risk associated with a mid-range score.\n\nWe were forced to keep **Braden Montgomery** on the bench, though he was the closest to cracking the starting nine. His score of 36.49 fell just short of our 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold, largely due to a tough matchup against a 3.41 xERA arm in Weathers, which erased his potential platoon and park advantages. Elsewhere, we are navigating the landscape without **Bryce Harper**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, and **Yainer Diaz** due to team off-days, and we continue to monitor the status of **Jonathan Aranda** and **JJ Bleday**. **Jonathan Aranda** is being started despite a difficult park and opposing pitcher because his 12% dynamic platoon edge and promotion to the #2 spot provide enough upside to squeeze past the competition. Conversely, **JJ Bleday**\u2019s 14% platoon penalty against a right-handed arm is a concern, but we are running him out there to chase his 47.92 projection in hopes that his spot in the #3 hole provides enough RBI opportunities to justify his roster slot over the remainder of the bench.",
